  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $-4\\in {-4,-2,8}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $-3\\in {-3,1,9}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $-2\\in {-4,-2,8}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $-1$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $0\\in {0,2,4}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $1\\in {-3,1,9}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $2\\in {0,2,4}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $3$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $4\\in {0,2,4}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $5\\in {5,6}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $6\\in {5,6}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $7$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $8\\in {-4,-2,8}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $9\\in {-3,1,9}\\,\u2713$\n\nThe elements $-1,$ $3,$ and $7$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${-1,3,7}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
